extract:
You are extracting constraints for academic search, not searching or answering the question. Return ONLY one valid JSON object with exactly these fields: topic, task, method, model, dataset, benchmark, domain, evaluation (strings), negative_constraints (array of strings), important_entities (array of strings). Every nonempty string MUST be an exact contiguous quote from the user question (case may differ). For multiple names use their complete original contiguous phrase, not a newly joined list. Use empty string or empty array for absent information. Preserve explicitly named datasets, benchmarks, methods and models. Put explicit comparisons and qualification conditions in evaluation; put exclusions and negative claims in negative_constraints. Do not invent names, synonyms, technical mechanisms, dates, or missing information. Do not output search queries or [Search] tags.
USER QUESTION:
{question}

facets:
Plan exactly five complementary academic search facets using ONLY the user question and its extracted constraints. Return ONLY a JSON array of five objects, each with facet (short unique English name), focus (English description), required_constraints (array of field names from the constraint object). Suggested roles are core_method, benchmark_dataset, application_task, technical_mechanism, broad_discovery. Adapt inapplicable roles: never invent a dataset, benchmark, method or mechanism. For a simple question, acknowledge limited distinct angles instead of fabricating new scope. A broad facet must keep the core topic and task. Preserve explicit entities, negation and comparisons across the portfolio. These are semantic angles, not five synonym rewrites. Do not generate final queries yet.
USER QUESTION:
{question}
EXTRACTED CONSTRAINTS:
{constraints}

generate:
Generate exactly five English academic search queries, one for each supplied facet in the same order. Return ONLY a JSON array of objects with query (string), facet (the exact supplied facet name), covered_constraints (array of constraint field names). Queries should be concise, preferably 6-24 words, suitable for arXiv/Google Scholar keyword search. Preserve important explicit entities and task restrictions; collectively cover ALL explicit datasets, benchmarks, methods, comparisons and exclusions. Do not weaken a comparison into a vague difficulty adjective. Do not introduce a new named model, method, benchmark, dataset or unsupported technical mechanism. Facets should explore complementary aspects rather than just reorder words or replace research with papers. For broad discovery retain the user's core task. No site/date filters; those belong to the later search layer. No [Search] tags, prose, retrieved papers, or answers. covered_constraints is your claim and will be audited separately.
USER QUESTION:
{question}
EXTRACTED CONSTRAINTS:
{constraints}
PLANNED FACETS:
{facets}
